{
  "title": "Web scrape status and import pages: restart, abort and stale-response handling",
  "description": "ScrapeStatusPage.tsx: polling starts only in onMount (115), so /scrape/a -> /scrape/b on the reused route doesn't restart it. \
The render relies on combination guards (pollError() && !job(), 196/205/225). \
After retryScrape succeeds pollError isn't cleared until the next update. \
ExpandedOutput allows loading + error + output together, and toggleExpand (129-153) has no staleness check, so a collapse or a retry clearing expanded (162-168) is undone when the old response writes back. \
ImportPage.tsx: no abort on unmount, so up to 10 minutes of polling continues after leaving and updateRow keeps writing (167-190); busy and fileError sit outside the RecipeStatus union; rows show 'Queued...' for the whole job without live status. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
